TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c02","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"The prime-counting observable is read directly off the sieve's incidence complex, with alternating signs from face dimension.","checksum":"7c6754b25b1b412b924df029d3acfa02fe887a63d3b62a21399f2876a529bfd1","id":"B1","limits":"Structural analogue only — her canonical form and positive region are absent.","type":"B","x":"D1's signed face-sum","y":"her step 3 ('read the amplitude off the geometry')"},{"buys":"The fast prime-counting algorithm was the link recursion all along.","checksum":"f362923163190e35bb8891c1190a4f724dac20338504eb1d9b0ee4cb943d4b78","id":"B2","limits":"Classical result in new clothes — proves the shape fits, not that the machinery transfers.","type":"B","x":"Lehmer φ-recursion (D2)","y":"her 'recursive facet residues' step"},{"buys":"Her generative insight — remove one generator, read the exact split, iterate to all orders — is the sieve's native operation.","checksum":"e96c2735902a0015e343a6fe898f6ec8e5308183459cdad2c220a1b81d5c68d1","id":"B3","limits":"Conceptual identification, not a new theorem.","type":"B","x":"Territory removal (D5)","y":"her all-order splits / multi-soft limits (arXiv:2405.09608)"},{"buys":"States the sieve in the language of binary geometries — the prerequisite for asking whether her algebraic machinery (positive parametrizations of u-variables) can be ported at all.","checksum":"46ec6df336f81e7ba2f799393a306321ad383d96dbeb24254f26f8b764365a69","id":"B4","limits":"Reformulation and analogy, not new prime information. Inverts her 'hidden zeros' picture: composites are the zero locus, primes its support. Zero-locus formulation verified to 60.","type":"B","x":"sieve's binary rule: 1_{prime}(n)+1_{shared}(n)=1 with shared(n)=∨_{p<n}(p|n); n composite ⟺ F(n)=0, n prime ⟺ F(n)>0 for F(n)=∏_{p<n}dist(n,pℤ)≥0","y":"her binary geometries' u_C+∏_D u_D^{n(C,D)}=1 (complementary on/off facet relations)"},{"checksum":"e5e85d6df7f42a234eb4386c340e3a98add824c87eaf6007734322ce3940044d","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"The empty face anchors the alternating sum","note":"In D1 the empty face (d=1, log 1=0) contributes no weight yet anchors the whole sum — the multiplicative identity structuring every term; formal shadow of 'every prime relates back to zero' via its spanning circle. The anchoring is exact; the 'relates back to zero' reading is interpretive.","status":"heuristic","type":"C"},{"checksum":"86f64a1231a0487639882b3b507cda2fe8606a87c4d4025407d3f30d3b7738ad","id":"C2","kind":"question","label":"Three precisely posed next questions","note":"(a) Is there a positive parametrization whose boundary strata are the territory incidences of Δ_x? (b) Partially answered by D4: the bare N→∞ limit trivializes — the limit object must be the weighted complex. (c) Do the sieve's binary relations admit positive variables with her exponent structure whose zero locus is the composites?","status":"unstated","type":"C"},{"checksum":"77d16a85435d723a16629915fc692d63579b674e3d45af637fe1c453fa023594","id":"C3","kind":"claim","label":"link({p}) recursion in Δ_x","note":"link({p}) in Δ_x = Δ_{⌊x/p⌋} minus p (exact recursion); link-face counts match Δ_{⌊x/p_a⌋} face counts; the integer bijection holds exactly.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"6c35671232b2e4e240ed1d65e74018d9f44b8be19c01be9769ca2d9e339db1b0","id":"C4","kind":"claim","label":"The sieve has no known positive region","note":"That gap stands. Her recipe's step 1 (find a positive geometric region) has no sieve analogue — what follows derives only her steps 2–4 in sieve shape.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"0d8557651998f8bc34b51c3f1a3ce0aeffb83c203fd6389118370420423fda34","id":"C5","kind":"question","label":"Is there a positive region with the weights as stratum residues?","note":"The weights are signed, alternating with face dimension — resonating with how a canonical form's residues alternate across boundary strata, but not positivity. The single sharpest question of the program.","status":"unstated","type":"C"},{"checksum":"42c49e8d0584c28a57482fad7f537b8df2e89e937f8416fcd7665e7a57b4b385","generates":[{"prescription":"⌊x/d⌋ counts the integers ≤ x divisible by d.","stage":"count"},{"prescription":"Group by n: inner sum over squarefree d|n of (−1)^{ω(d)+1} log d = −Σ_{d|n} μ(d) log d = Λ(n), via Möbius inversion.","stage":"group"},{"prescription":"Sum over n ≤ x to get ψ(x).","stage":"sum"}],"honest_boundary":"Classical theorem (Möbius inversion) in new clothes — the math is classical; the claim is that the prime-counting observable is read directly off the sieve's incidence complex, not that the identity is new.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D1","rule":"ψ(x) = Σ_{∅≠S face of Δ_x} (−1)^{|S|+1}·log(∏S)·⌊x/∏S⌋.","subtitle":"The observable as a signed face-sum (her step 3)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"exact identity at x=30,100,500","expected":"exact"}]},{"checksum":"80a4c36eda7a8844d1516de17ec52af698505d3edb36eb13354f2fe9991a7498","generates":[{"prescription":"The integers newly shared when territory p_a is added are exactly {p_a·m : m ≤ x/p_a unshared by the first a−1 territories}.","stage":"delete-link"},{"prescription":"These are in bijection with the cone S ↦ S ∪ {p_a} over link({p_a}) = Δ_{⌊x/p_a⌋}.","stage":"bijection"}],"honest_boundary":"Classical (Lehmer 1959) reframed — the fast prime-counting algorithm was the link recursion all along; proves the shape fits, not that her machinery transfers.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D2","rule":"φ(x,a)=φ(x,a−1)−φ(x/p_a,a−1); π(x)=φ(x,a)+a−1−P₂(x,a); the two terms are the complex's deletion and link.","subtitle":"Lehmer's recursion is the link recursion (her step 4)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"link-face counts vs Δ_{⌊x/p_a⌋} face counts","expected":"match"},{"check":"integer bijection","expected":"exact"}]},{"checksum":"3f331ad708bb4af1e86ee844f3fee910ec88daa97fd8da5bf17a5451beab3b41","generates":[{"prescription":"As x→∞ every finite prime set satisfies ∏S≤x — Δ_∞ is the infinite simplex: contractible, no topology; the geometry must live in the WEIGHTS (her objects are fixed polytopes; the sieve's object is a process — the filtration itself).","stage":"bare limit"},{"prescription":"ψ(x)/x = Σ_{∏S≤x} w(S)·(⌊x/∏S⌋/(x/∏S)) — the floor function is a cutoff that tends to 1.","stage":"weighted sum"},{"prescription":"The Dirichlet GF of the weights is −ζ′(s)/ζ(s)²; the rate of S(X)→1 — the face-sum error — is governed by the zeros of ζ (explicit formula).","stage":"regulators"}],"honest_boundary":"Σ→1 is equivalent to PNT — classical, reframed; the zeros are NEEDED as regulators of the infinite sum, but deriving them from the geometry remains open (beachhead #2).","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D4","rule":"w(S)=(−1)^{|S|+1}·log(∏S)/∏S; Σ_{∏S≤X} w(S)→1 (X→∞); Σ_S w(S)/∏S^{s−1} = −ζ′(s)/ζ(s)².","subtitle":"Weighted infinite complex: PNT as total weight 1 (the N→∞ limit)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"S(X) at X=10³,10⁴,10⁵,5·10⁵,10⁶,2·10⁶","expected":"0.969931, 1.019210, 1.005585, 0.999922, 0.997215, 1.001658 → 1"},{"check":"GF vs ζ′/ζ² at s=1.01…1.20","expected":"agree to ~4 digits"}]},{"checksum":"59f515ebeac22e26dfecbfdd7ec7e8b23cbbd4c495d067da0159f0444e73ae50","generates":[{"prescription":"'Take prime p_a soft' = stop sieving by p_a; the removed stratum φ(x/p_a,a−1) is the same kind of object at a smaller scale — her 'soft factor × lower-point amplitude'.","stage":"soft limit"},{"prescription":"Iterate the removal over all a: the full inclusion–exclusion is recovered — the face-sum of D1 — her 'all-order' in sieve language.","stage":"iterate"}],"honest_boundary":"A conceptual identification, not a new theorem — it is D2's recursion read through her lens (numerics already verified under D2); the sieve was already doing splits before we knew her name for them.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D5","rule":"φ(x,a)=φ(x,a−1)−φ(x/p_a,a−1): full count = count with p_a removed − the removed stratum; iterating over all a recovers the D1 face-sum.","subtitle":"Territory removal as soft limit / splitting (her all-order splits)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"soft-limit split as removed-stratum bijection (link-face counts vs Δ_{⌊x/p_a⌋} face counts)","expected":"match — verification carried by D2 (integer bijection holds exactly)"},{"check":"iteration over all a recovers the full inclusion–exclusion / D1 face-sum","expected":"exact — D1 verified at x=30,100,500"}]},{"checksum":"fd9c894dff86dc1b84efde59cf44e862b3e1136d67801bbceaa04ace1a3f1352","from":"D1","id":"L1","rel":"depends_on","to":"D4","type":"L"},{"checksum":"535bfa93744ab81df928aebfafb153a4808d2fb747e1cdbcd8c3f14831c5764a","from":"D2","id":"L2","rel":"depends_on","to":"D5","type":"L"},{"checksum":"6e171c8059c865ab75ece05d5384060f4e0ba2d3763e2064a5e55c4cd3b071cf","from":"B1","id":"L3","rel":"supports","to":"V1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"6c6f18643704b89c40025773a3ce7eb30d9eecab375ad7e5914f7b525b18e8c4","from":"D4","id":"L4","rel":"causes","to":"C5","type":"L"},{"checksum":"fd0d6c1f17d0681abe53c6847d9e9cfccc005e78513ba548ede10f63fbeb76ac","consequence":"D1–D5 are classical results in new clothes; they prove the shape fits, not that the machinery transfers. Next questions (a) and (c) stand open; the program is a counting problem of her kind (arXiv:2309.15913) with steps 2–4 exact and step 1 (positive region) missing.","id":"V1","note":"Have: the sieve's output (ψ, π) as (i) a signed face-sum over Δ_x and (ii) a link-recursive computation — her recipe's steps 2–4 with exact analogues, minus the positive region and canonical form. Don't have: the positive region, the canonical form, or any new consequence for prime densities.","status":"exact","subject":"What D1–D5 buy, and what they don't","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","B3":"B","B4":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","C3":"C","C4":"C","C5":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D4":"D","D5":"D","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","V1":"V"},"wire_checksum":"6c51422988871ded5358fe5161d7520a250add1ca8829dba8f06294e66126a69"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1